# A wider heater spreads the same power over more oxide: the waveguide sees less of it.
# Reference: the same mesh solved with a sparse direct solver in SciPy.
title Heater 10 um wide
grid dx=0.25 dy=0.25
window width=60 ymin=-10 ymax=5
layer si -10 0
layer sio2 0 5
rect si -0.25 0.25 2 2.25
rect tin -5 5 4 4.25
heater h xmin=-5 xmax=5 ymin=4 ymax=4.25 power=0.1
probe wg xmin=-0.25 xmax=0.25 ymin=2 ymax=2.25
expect response wg h 109.533756 1e-7
expect pi_power wg h 38.0400236 1e-7
expect peak 21.0057074 1e-7
expect balance 1e-9
expect cells 14400
